! agent_p125.strap -- MCP "THE RECEPTOR", printed page 125.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.132, header READ and not assumed:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID EB000151   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 125", and
! the column-heading row repeats "LOCATION 216056" on the right.
! (The volume's OCR index, docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt line 29,
! titles the EB deck "THE RECEPTOR".)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX ROWS, EVERY ONE OF THEM CODE.  No comment cards, no
! SYN rows, no DD.  First printed location 216056.40 (line 1), last
! 216121.00 (line 56); line 56 is a half word, so the counter
! leaves this page at 216121.40.
!
! THE ADDRESS CHAIN CLOSES END TO END over all fifty-six rows:
! every printed address plus the row's own length (half word, or
! full word where the BINARY OUTPUT column prints two half words)
! equals the next row's printed address, with no gap and no
! overlap.  That is the page's internal check and it passes.
!
! The page is the tail of the RECEPTOR's unit-hunt and its two
! wait loops:
!   lines  1- 4  index set-up over the unit-area table ($11).
!   lines  5- 7  K HUNT / K HEX: scan the table for a unit whose
!                REWIND or MOUNT bit is on, branching to K STAB.
!   lines  8-10  pull the unit number out of S UNIT and preset the
!                retry count ($11) and $6 from K REP.
!   lines 11-19  K PUNT: a LOC(SEOP) control operation, then the
!                standard "wait for EKJ, count down, give up"
!                three-row loop, then RCLRUK -- save the IC in
!                KCBJR and go clear the control word.
!   lines 20-31  K NET: the same shape around a CCW (-WAIT FOR END
!                OP), then the SEOP / stray-interrupt tests and the
!                CI0001 connective that builds a six-bit pattern.
!   lines 32-35  RINTOK: step $11 and re-enter RNTMCP+1.0.
!   lines 36-40  K K SET: return if a stray CS interrupt, set the
!                K CS Q bit, test S OWNER, go to K NORM.
!   lines 41-56  K STAB (-TEST IF UNIT IS READY) and KSTAG: a third
!                and fourth copy of the LOC/CCW wait loop.
!
! FOUR COMMENT-COLUMN ENTRIES, and they are the page's English
! oracle (docs/transcription_workflow.md):
!   line 20  -WAIT FOR END OP
!   line 27  -IF SEOP BIT ON, LOOP      <- settles SEOP, not SECP
!   line 36  -RETURN IF STRAY CS
!   line 41  -TEST IF UNIT IS READY
!
! THREE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISKS, recorded and not explained:
! lines 2, 21 and 37 print a bare "*" after the location, the same
! mark printed p.103 line 48 and printed pp.3/37 carry.  No
! compiled bit changes and none of them is checked here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS ASSERTED, NOT READ.  THIS IS THE PAGE'S ONE
! REAL HOLE. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE PRINTS NO "SLC" ROW AT ALL, and printed pp.121, 122,
! 123 and 124 have not been transcribed, so the counter arriving
! here cannot be compared against anything.  The SLC written below
! is line 1's own printed LOCATION restated so the deck assembles
! standalone.
!
! docs/transcription_workflow.md "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" #2
! applies in full: a hard SLC OVERRIDES the arriving counter
! silently, so all fifty-six !CHECK rows below would pass at any
! origin.  They verify the page's INTERNAL consistency and its
! externals; they do not verify the backward join to printed p.120.
! THE BACKWARD JOIN IS OPEN.
!
! THE FORWARD JOIN IS CLOSED, and for free.  Printed p.126's first
! row is "216121.40 * 216332.30 80 216116.74 02  BB,K RECEP.24,
! K STAG" (docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt line 6552).  Line 56
! here is a half word at 216121.00, so this page hands over
! 216121.40 and p.126 prints exactly that.  Note also that p.126's
! row branches to K STAG, which is DEFINED on this page (line 52,
! 216116.40) -- a second, independent tie between the two pages.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NAMES DEFINED HERE (9)
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! K HUNT 216060.40, K HEX 216062.40, K PUNT 216065.00,
! RCLRUK 216070.40, K NET 216072.00, RINTOK 216102.00,
! K K SET 216104.40, K STAB 216110.40, KSTAG 216116.40.
!
! BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
! printed p.2.  This page prints the SAME symbol both ways on
! purpose -- "K REP" on lines 11, 20, 43 and "KREP" on lines 9 and
! 52; "K K SET" on line 36 and "KKSET" on line 32; "K CS Q" on
! line 38 and "KCSQ" on line 37; "K STAB" on lines 5/6/41/46 and
! "KSTAB" on line 51; "K RECEP" on lines 21/25/27/53 and "KRECEP"
! on line 32 -- which is itself the proof that the blanks are not
! part of the name.
!
! >>> THE ONE NAME THAT RESTS ON INK ALONE IS RCLRUK. <<<  It is
! referenced only by line 30 of its own page; the volume OCR
! garbles both instances ("REE RUK" at line 6511).  Two agreeing
! instances on one page is INTERNAL consistency, not an external
! check -- the letters could be jointly wrong.  Read at 800 dpi
! and recorded as read; no !CHECK can test a spelling.
! Every other name has an off-page witness:
!   K HEX   -- printed p.126 line 2 and p.127 line 14 branch to it
!              (OCR lines 6554, 6569, both "216062.74").
!   KSTAG   -- printed p.126 line 1 (OCR 6552).
!   K K SET -- line 32 of this page spells it KKSET.
!   K CS Q  -- its own defining card, OCR line 6616.
!   K HUNT / K PUNT / K NET / K STAB / RINTOK -- referenced from
!              this page's own rows AND, for K STAB, from p.126.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- WHAT IS PINNED AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) PINNED TO THE BIT.  A VFL / BRANCH-ON-BIT / connective
!     operand field is a 24-bit BIT address, so the printed row
!     fixes the whole value, offset included:
!       K RECEP 216332.00 -- and its own card is printed:
!            "216332.00  ... K RECEP XW,0"  (OCR line 6770),
!            corroborated by .19/.21/.24 offsets on lines 25/32/27.
!       K CS Q  216171.00 -- card "216171.00 000000.00+ K CS Q
!            VF,0" (OCR line 6616); line 37 uses KCSQ.31.
!       S REW .52, S MOUNT .51, S UNIT .56, S OWNER .32, all bit
!            offsets inside the unit-area table entry.
!
! (b) HALF-WORD ONLY BY BACK-DERIVATION FROM A PRINTED BRANCH --
!     bit offsets 0-31 all encode identically (workflow doc, "WHAT
!     THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" #1), so the ".00"/".40" below is the
!     HALF WORD and the bits inside it are a CONVENTION, not a
!     reading.  EACH ONE IS DISCHARGED BY A DEFINING CARD found by
!     greping the volume OCR for the octal address:
!       K REJT  221300.00  OCR 9561 "221300.00 ... K REJT LVI,14,"
!       K CLEAR 221302.40  OCR 9569 "221302.40 000036.03 02 K CLEAR"
!       K CBJ R 221313.40  OCR 9590 "221313.40 221263.10 00 K CBJ R"
!       K SOS   221274.00  OCR 9549 "221274.00 * ... K SOS LVI,14,"
!       K NORM  215776.00  OCR 6405 "215776.00 000036.37 02 K NORM"
!       K SUPP  216242.00  OCR 6677 "216242.00 216246.70 00 K SUPP"
!       RNTMCP  216133.00  OCR 6569 "216133.00 216332.25 80 RNTMCP"
!     So every half-word external here has its own printed card at
!     the address this page's branch implies; none of them is a
!     tautology off this page alone.
!
! (c) K REP IS NOT AN ADDRESS.  It is a COUNT, decimal 30.  Two
!     witnesses, neither of them this page: printed p.129's K CLEAR
!     card is "LCI,1,K REP" compiling 000036.03 02 (OCR 9569), and
!     printed p.124's K NORM card is the same instruction written
!     with the literal, "LCI,15,30", compiling 000036.37 02 (OCR
!     6405).  0o36 = 30.  Written here as "SYN, 30"; measured, that
!     reproduces lines 9/11/20/43/52 exactly.
!
! (d) SPELLINGS REUSED FROM A LANDED PAGE, deliberately, as
!     tests/check_symbol_spellings.py asks.  S UN A, S REW,
!     S MOUNT, S UNIT and S OWNER are all defined on printed p.99
!     (decks/mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap lines 20, 43, 42, 39, 30) and
!     this deck copies those exact spellings and values -- SUNA 0.0,
!     SREW 0.52, SMOUNT 0.51, SUNIT 0.56, SOWNER 0.32.  SMOUNT at
!     0.51 is additionally carried, at the same value, by the decks
!     for printed pp.70, 75, 79, 97 and 98, so this is not even a
!     tail-scope repeat: it is one symbol with one value.
!     S CS INT is printed p.103's S CS INT (SCOMRG bit 7) at
!     215001.07, and line 36 of this page prints that address --
!     an independent confirmation of p.103's bit-level layout.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- FOUR BYTES THE INK COULD NOT SETTLE, SETTLED BY WHAT
! PRODUCED THEM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs as badly as any in the volume: its
! own column heading prints "LCCATICN", and rows print "COCC10.26",
! "COCCOO.64", "2160C65.1C CO".  Every one of those is an OCTAL
! field and cannot hold a C, so they are 0 with certainty -- but
! that is NOT a licence over the hex byte (workflow doc: ink varies
! per CHARACTER).  The four doubtful bytes were settled on the
! ENCODING, and then measured:
!
!   line  3  V+,11,$L      reads "BO"/"80" -> it is B0.  A direct
!            index half word puts J in bits 19-22 and the 5-bit op
!            code in bits 23-27, so V+ (01011) lands its low four
!            bits in the byte's HIGH nibble: B.  Line 1's LC
!            (00101) gives 5 and prints "50"; line 10's LV,6
!            (00011) gives 3 and prints "30".  Assembled: B0.
!            THIS IS THE p.95 HAZARD RUNNING THE OTHER WAY -- the
!            glyph really is a B.
!   line 34  V+I,$11,1.0   reads "C5"/"05" -> it is 05.  An
!            IMMEDIATE index op puts its 4-bit code in bits 28-31,
!            the byte's LOW nibble, and bits 24-27 are zero: V+I is
!            0101 -> 05.  Assembled: 05.
!   line 42  V-I,2,1.0     reads "CD"/"0D" -> it is 0D, by the same
!            rule (V-I = 1101), and line 4 is the SAME operation
!            with the same operand and prints a clean 0D.
!   line 11  LCI,1,K REP   reads "C2"/"02" -> it is 02 (LCI =
!            0010), and lines 20, 43 and 52 print the identical
!            instruction with a clean 02.
! The volume OCR reads "C2" for a LCI row elsewhere (line 9569),
! which is exactly the "comparing against other rows is weaker
! still" trap; the encoder is the arbiter and all four assemble to
! the printed word.
!
! C/D and B/8 were checked at 900 dpi over the whole BINARY OUTPUT
! column.  The only B's on the page are line 3's B0 and the 8B/8A/
! 8E index bytes, every one of which is forced by the ($11)/($10)/
! ($14) written in its own statement.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION -- ONE, AND IT IS THE "*I+" GAP AGAIN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 28 PRINTS "CI0001(BU,6),(.5,2)110001" AND strap_asm REJECTS
! IT: KeyError 'CI0001' out of VFL_INT_CODES.  THE PRINTED FORM WAS
! TESTED FIRST, as the brief requires, and that is the measured
! failure.
!
! The cause is known and already written down in strap_asm.py: the
! immediate suffix "I" (C22-6531 Appendix A footnote 3, reached for
! connectives through footnote 10, which strap_asm quotes at
! classify_connective's caller) is accepted as a SUFFIX --
! "C0001I" -- but IBM also writes it INFIX, inside the two-
! character operation.  strap_asm carries exactly one such spelling,
! VFL_INFIX_IMMEDIATE = {"*I+": "*+I"}, from printed pp.95/96.
! "CI0001" is the same phenomenon on a connective and it has an
! independent primary-source witness OUTSIDE this listing:
! 7030 Performance Characteristics Vol.2 (Mar 61) prints
! "CI0011(BU, 8), (16)A, -8" in a worked program
! (docs/ocr/7030_Performance_Characteristics_Vol2_Mar61.txt:1634),
! beside "LI(BU, 8), (16)A" -- the same I, infix, on a connective.
!
! THE SUBSTITUTION IS BIT-IDENTICAL AND MEASURED.  Written
! "CI0001(BU,6),(.5,2)110001" the row assembles to
! 610000.00 80  406000.02 70 -- the printed word, both half words,
! exactly.  The deck therefore writes C0001I and keeps the printed
! CI0001 in the row's !CHECK note.  NOTHING UNDER strap/ WAS
! MODIFIED; this is reported, not fixed.  The fix, if someone wants
! it, is one line in VFL_INFIX_IMMEDIATE.
!
! NOTHING ELSE ON THE PAGE WAS SUBSTITUTED.  Every other printed
! spelling was fed to strap_asm as printed and accepted, including
! the ones worth naming because they look like they would not be:
!   LOC(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0($6)   line 12 -- the IO form, channel
!                                 field written as printed
!   LOC(SEOP),0.0($14),0.($2)    line 44 -- the bare trailing dot
!   (.5,2)110001                 line 28 -- parenthetical entry,
!                                 radix 2, as on printed p.117
!   BZEKJZ / BZCBJZ / BZBZ / BZB / BRZ / CB- / SIC / SC / V+I /
!   V-I / CM0000 / C0011         all as printed
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---- EXTERNALS, with the printed address each was read from -----

SUNA    SYN(BU,25), 0.0              ! dds (BU,25) added 2026-11-02: p.99
                                     ! line 19 declares S UN AA (BU,25) and
                                     ! line 20 aliases S UN A to it, so this
                                     ! literal spelling must carry the dds
                                     ! the alias would have inherited.
                                     ! Original note: p.99 line 20 (SUNA SYN,SUNAA,
                                      !   SUNAA SYN(BU,25),0.0)
SREW    SYN(BU,1), 0.52              ! p.99 line 43; line 5 here
SMOUNT  SYN(BU,1), 0.51              ! p.99 line 42; line 6 here
SUNIT   SYN(BU,3), 0.56              ! p.99 line 39; line 8 here
SOWNER  SYN(BU,1), 0.32              ! p.99 line 30; line 39 here
SCSINT  SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.07      ! p.103 line 17 (SCOMRG bit 7)
KREP    SYN, 30                      ! A COUNT, not an address --
                                      !   OCR 9569 / 6405, see above
KRECEP  SYN, (8)216332.0             ! card OCR 6770 "K RECEP XW,0"
KCSQ    SYN, (8)216171.0             ! card OCR 6616 "K CS Q VF,0"
KREJT   SYN, (8)221300.0             ! card OCR 9561; HALF WORD only
KCLEAR  SYN, (8)221302.40            ! card OCR 9569; HALF WORD only
KCBJR   SYN, (8)221313.40            ! card OCR 9590; HALF WORD only
KSOS    SYN, (8)221274.0             ! card OCR 9549; HALF WORD only
KNORM   SYN, (8)215776.0             ! card OCR 6405; HALF WORD only
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! card OCR 6677; HALF WORD only
RNTMCP  SYN, (8)216133.0             ! card OCR 6569; HALF WORD only

